export const LOOKALIKES = [
	{"ids":["alaskan-malamute","siberian-husky","alaskan-klee-kai"],"tell":"The Malamute is the big one: heavier, brown-eyed, with a plumed tail carried over the back. The Husky is medium and lighter, often blue-eyed, with a brush tail. The Klee Kai is a small Husky."},
	{"ids":["golden-retriever","labrador","flat-coated-retriever","toller"],"tell":"Coat first: the Labrador's is short and dense with an otter tail; the Golden's long, wavy and gold; the Flat-coat's long, flat and black or liver. The Toller is much smaller, red, with white on the face, chest and feet."},
	{"ids":["labrador","chesapeake","curly-coated-retriever"],"tell":"The Labrador's coat is short and smooth; the Chesapeake's is wavy and oily, with yellow eyes; the Curly is covered in tight curls except on the face."},
	{"ids":["german-shepherd","malinois","dutch-shepherd","tervuren"],"tell":"The German Shepherd is longer and deeper, with a sloping back and a saddle. The Malinois is lighter and square, fawn with a black mask. The Dutch Shepherd is built like the Malinois but always brindle. The Tervuren is a long-haired fawn Belgian."},
	{"ids":["groenendael","tervuren","malinois","laekenois"],"tell":"The four Belgian Shepherds share one body: long black is the Groenendael, long fawn the Tervuren, short fawn the Malinois, rough fawn the Laekenois."},
	{"ids":["german-shepherd","white-swiss-shepherd","czechoslovakian-wolfdog","saarloos-wolfdog"],"tell":"A white German-Shepherd-shaped dog is the White Swiss Shepherd. The wolfdogs are leaner and wolf-grey with light eyes: the Czechoslovakian has a pale mask and short ears, the Saarloos is taller and lankier."},
	{"ids":["rough-collie","shetland-sheepdog","smooth-collie"],"tell":"The Sheltie looks like a small Rough Collie: around 35 cm at the shoulder against the Collie's 60. The Smooth Collie is a Rough Collie with a short coat."},
	{"ids":["border-collie","australian-shepherd","mini-american-shepherd","australian-kelpie"],"tell":"The Border Collie has a long tail and is usually black and white. The Aussie is often merle with copper trim and a bob tail. The Miniature American Shepherd is a smaller Aussie. The Kelpie is lean and fox-faced with a short coat."},
	{"ids":["pembroke-corgi","cardigan-corgi","swedish-vallhund","lancashire-heeler"],"tell":"The Pembroke has no tail and pointed ears; the Cardigan has a long fox tail and rounder ears. The Vallhund is wolf-grey. The Lancashire Heeler is black and tan."},
	{"ids":["australian-cattle-dog","stumpy-tail-cattle-dog"],"tell":"Both are speckled blue or red. The Stumpy Tail is leggier and born with a bob tail; the Cattle Dog has a full tail."},
	{"ids":["bulldog","french-bulldog","boston-terrier","continental-bulldog"],"tell":"The Bulldog is big, low and wide with rose ears. The Frenchie is small with bat ears. The Boston is leaner, black-and-white in a tuxedo pattern. The Continental Bulldog has a longer muzzle and legs."},
	{"ids":["american-bulldog","dogo-argentino","boxer"],"tell":"The Dogo is pure white and sleek. The American Bulldog is mostly white with patches and a broader head. The Boxer is fawn or brindle with a black mask and an underbite."},
	{"ids":["staffordshire-bull-terrier","american-staffordshire","pit-bull","american-bully"],"tell":"Size and shape: the Staffy is the smallest and most compact; the AmStaff is taller and heavier; the Pit Bull is leaner and leggier; the American Bully is the widest and lowest, with a huge head."},
	{"ids":["bull-terrier","miniature-bull-terrier"],"tell":"The same egg-shaped head: only the size differs."},
	{"ids":["dobermann","german-pinscher","miniature-pinscher","manchester-terrier","english-toy-terrier","prague-ratter"],"tell":"All sleek black-and-tan. The Dobermann is large; the German Pinscher medium; the Min Pin tiny and high-stepping. The Manchester has a longer wedge head; the English Toy Terrier is a toy Manchester; the Prague Ratter is tiny with a round head."},
	{"ids":["miniature-schnauzer","standard-schnauzer","giant-schnauzer"],"tell":"The three schnauzers differ in size: small, medium and large."},
	{"ids":["akita","american-akita","shiba-inu"],"tell":"The Japanese Akita is fox-like, in red, sesame or white, with no black mask. The American Akita is heavier with a bear-like head and often a black mask. The Shiba is small."},
	{"ids":["shiba-inu","jindo","finnish-spitz","kishu","shikoku","kai-ken","hokkaido"],"tell":"The Finnish Spitz is fox-red all over with a long plumed tail. The Shiba is small with white urajiro. The Jindo and Kishu are bigger, often white. The Shikoku is sesame; the Kai is always brindle; the Hokkaido is the sturdiest."},
	{"ids":["samoyed","american-eskimo","japanese-spitz","german-spitz","volpino","kishu"],"tell":"White spitzes: the Samoyed is the biggest with its smile. The American Eskimo has black lips and nose and a lion ruff. The Japanese Spitz is small and pointed. The Volpino is Italian and smaller still. The German Spitz is fluffy and round."},
	{"ids":["pomeranian","german-spitz","keeshond","volpino"],"tell":"The Pomeranian is the tiny one. The German Spitz is bigger, in white, black or orange. The Keeshond is grey with dark spectacles. The Volpino is small and usually white."},
	{"ids":["keeshond","norwegian-elkhound","eurasier","swedish-vallhund"],"tell":"The Keeshond has spectacles and a heavy mane. The Elkhound is grey with a black muzzle and a tight curl. The Eurasier is calmer-faced and comes in many colours. The Vallhund is low like a corgi."},
	{"ids":["jamthund","norwegian-elkhound","black-norwegian-elkhound","karelian-bear-dog"],"tell":"The Jämthund is taller, with cream cheeks and throat. The Norwegian Elkhound is grey with a darker saddle; the Black Elkhound is all black. The Karelian is black with white markings."},
	{"ids":["east-siberian-laika","west-siberian-laika","russo-european-laika","yakutian-laika"],"tell":"The West Siberian is wolf-like, often white or grey. The East Siberian is larger and heavier. The Russo-European is black and white. The Yakutian is a white sled dog with patches, often blue-eyed."},
	{"ids":["maltese","bichon-frise","bolognese","coton-de-tulear","havanese"],"tell":"The small white dogs differ by coat: Maltese straight and silky to the floor; Bichon curly and trimmed round; Bolognese fluffy and loose; Coton soft like cotton. The Havanese is silky and wavy and comes in many colours."},
	{"ids":["shih-tzu","lhasa-apso","tibetan-terrier","pekingese"],"tell":"The Shih Tzu has a short, square face; the Lhasa a longer muzzle and a harder coat. The Tibetan Terrier is bigger and shaggier. The Pekingese is low, with a flat face and a mane."},
	{"ids":["yorkshire-terrier","australian-silky","biewer","australian-terrier"],"tell":"The Yorkie's coat is long, silky and steel blue and tan; the Silky's is shorter and doesn't reach the floor; the Biewer adds white. The Australian Terrier is sturdier with a ruff and a harsh coat."},
	{"ids":["cavalier","king-charles-spaniel","papillon","japanese-chin"],"tell":"The Cavalier has a flat skull and a short muzzle; the King Charles a domed head and a flat, upturned face. The Papillon has big butterfly ears. The Chin is flat-faced with wide-set eyes."},
	{"ids":["english-cocker","american-cocker","english-springer","welsh-springer","field-spaniel","sussex-spaniel"],"tell":"The American Cocker is smallest, with a domed head and heavy coat. The English Cocker has a longer muzzle. The English Springer is taller, liver or black with white; the Welsh Springer red and white. The Field is long and low; the Sussex low, heavy and golden-liver."},
	{"ids":["greyhound","whippet","italian-greyhound","galgo","magyar-agar"],"tell":"Size first: Greyhound large, Whippet medium, Italian Greyhound toy. The Galgo has a longer, finer head; the Magyar Agár is sturdier."},
	{"ids":["irish-wolfhound","deerhound"],"tell":"Both are tall and rough-coated. The Wolfhound is heavier and more powerful; the Deerhound leaner and more Greyhound-like, usually blue-grey."},
	{"ids":["saluki","afghan-hound","borzoi","sloughi","azawakh","kazakh-tazy"],"tell":"The Afghan is covered in long silk with a topknot. The Borzoi has a long Roman nose and a silky coat. The Saluki is smooth with feathered ears and tail; the Sloughi and Azawakh have no feathering, and the Azawakh is very tall and thin. The Tazy has feathered ears and a ring tail."},
	{"ids":["pharaoh-hound","ibizan-hound","cirneco","podenco-canario"],"tell":"Big upright ears on all four. The Ibizan is tallest and red-and-white; the Pharaoh is solid tan-red with amber eyes; the Cirneco is a small Pharaoh; the Canario sits between them in size."},
	{"ids":["beagle","harrier","english-foxhound","american-foxhound","estonian-hound","beagle-harrier"],"tell":"Same pattern, different size: the Beagle is small, the Harrier medium, the Foxhounds large (the American taller and lighter than the English)."},
	{"ids":["basset-hound","basset-artesien-normand","basset-bleu-de-gascogne","drever","westphalian-dachsbracke"],"tell":"The Basset Hound is the heaviest, with loose skin and droopy eyes. The Artésien Normand is lighter and tricolour or fawn. The Basset Bleu is blue-mottled. The Drever and Westphalian Dachsbracke are leggier with white blazes."},
	{"ids":["pbgv","gbgv","basset-fauve","griffon-fauve","briquet-griffon-vendeen","grand-griffon-vendeen"],"tell":"The Vendée griffons grow with the name: Petit Basset smallest, Grand Basset longer-legged, Briquet medium, Grand Griffon tall. The Breton ones are fawn: Basset Fauve low, Griffon Fauve leggy."},
	{"ids":["bloodhound","black-and-tan-coonhound","hanover-hound"],"tell":"The Bloodhound has deep wrinkles and drooping eyes. The Black and Tan Coonhound is sleeker with long ears. The Hanover Hound is red-brindle with a mask."},
	{"ids":["bluetick-coonhound","american-english-coonhound","treeing-walker","redbone-coonhound","plott-hound"],"tell":"The Bluetick is dark blue-mottled. The American English is ticked with white. The Treeing Walker is white with black and tan. The Redbone is solid red; the Plott is brindle."},
	{"ids":["vizsla","wirehaired-vizsla","rhodesian-ridgeback","redbone-coonhound"],"tell":"The Vizsla is lean and golden-rust with a red nose. The Wirehaired Vizsla has a beard. The Ridgeback is bigger, wheaten, with the ridge. The Redbone has long hound ears."},
	{"ids":["weimaraner","german-shorthaired-pointer","pointer","braque-francais"],"tell":"The Weimaraner is all silver-grey. The German Shorthair is liver or liver-ticked. The Pointer has a dished face and patches on white. The Braque Français has liver ticking and longer ears."},
	{"ids":["irish-setter","irish-red-white-setter","english-setter","gordon-setter"],"tell":"Colour tells setters apart: solid red Irish, red-and-white Irish, flecked English, black-and-tan Gordon."},
	{"ids":["german-wirehaired-pointer","wirehaired-pointing-griffon","spinone","cesky-fousek","slovak-roughhaired-pointer","german-roughhaired-pointer"],"tell":"Wire-coated pointers: the Drahthaar is liver-roan with a beard; the Korthals Griffon is shaggier and grey-brown; the Spinone is big and kind-faced, white or roan; the Fousek is Czech brown-roan; the Slovak is grey-roan with amber eyes."},
	{"ids":["large-munsterlander","small-munsterlander","german-longhaired-pointer"],"tell":"The Large Münsterländer is black and white; the Small is brown and white and smaller; the Longhaired Pointer is liver."},
	{"ids":["smooth-fox-terrier","wire-fox-terrier","jack-russell","parson-russell","rat-terrier","toy-fox-terrier"],"tell":"The Fox Terriers are square and taller; smooth or wire. The Jack Russell is longer than tall; the Parson is the leggy Russell. The Rat Terrier has big ears and a pied coat; the Toy Fox Terrier is tiny."},
	{"ids":["rat-terrier","teddy-roosevelt-terrier","american-hairless-terrier"],"tell":"The Teddy Roosevelt is a short-legged Rat Terrier; the American Hairless has no coat."},
	{"ids":["airedale","welsh-terrier","lakeland-terrier","irish-terrier"],"tell":"The Airedale is the big one; the Welsh a smaller Airedale; the Lakeland smaller still and comes in more colours. The Irish is all red."},
	{"ids":["norwich-terrier","norfolk-terrier","cairn-terrier","border-terrier"],"tell":"The Norwich has upright ears and the Norfolk folded ones. The Cairn is shaggier with a fox face. The Border has an otter head."},
	{"ids":["west-highland","cairn-terrier","scottish-terrier","sealyham"],"tell":"The Westie is white with a round head. A white Cairn has a foxier face. The Scottie is long-headed and usually black. The Sealyham is white with folded ears and a long beard."},
	{"ids":["bernese","greater-swiss","entlebucher","appenzeller"],"tell":"The Bernese is the long-haired one. The Greater Swiss is big and short-coated; the Appenzeller medium with a curled tail; the Entlebucher smallest, often with a bob tail."},
	{"ids":["mastiff","bullmastiff","dogue-de-bordeaux","cane-corso","neapolitan-mastiff","boerboel"],"tell":"The Mastiff is huge with a black mask. The Bullmastiff is smaller and compact. The Dogue de Bordeaux is red with a huge head and no black mask. The Cane Corso is athletic, often black or grey. The Neapolitan is draped in folds. The Boerboel is square and muscular."},
	{"ids":["pyrenean-mountain-dog","maremma","kuvasz","slovak-cuvac","tatra-shepherd"],"tell":"White mountain guardians: the Great Pyrenees has double dewclaws and often grey marks on the head. The Maremma is rough-coated with a bear head. The Kuvasz is wavy. The Cuvac and Tatra are lighter-built, the Tatra with a thick mane."},
	{"ids":["pyrenean-mastiff","spanish-mastiff"],"tell":"The Pyrenean Mastiff is white with sharp patches and a longer coat; the Spanish Mastiff is usually fawn or brindle, with heavier loose skin."},
	{"ids":["newfoundland","landseer"],"tell":"The Newfoundland is usually black; the Landseer is white with black patches and taller."},
	{"ids":["kangal","anatolian-shepherd","central-asian-shepherd","caucasian-shepherd"],"tell":"The Kangal is pale fawn with a black mask. The Anatolian comes in more colours. The Central Asian is massive and short-coated; the Caucasian has a thick bear-like coat."},
	{"ids":["mioritic-shepherd","carpathian-shepherd","bucovina-shepherd","romanian-raven-shepherd"],"tell":"The Mioritic is shaggy white or pale grey; the Carpathian wolf-coloured; the Bucovina white with patches; the Raven black."},
	{"ids":["komondor","puli","bergamasco","spanish-water-dog"],"tell":"Corded coats: the Komondor is huge and white; the Puli medium and usually black; the Bergamasco grey with flat mats; the Spanish Water Dog woolly and smaller."},
	{"ids":["poodle","portuguese-water-dog","lagotto","barbet","spanish-water-dog"],"tell":"Curly water dogs: the Poodle is clipped and elegant; the Portie is sturdier, often in a lion clip; the Lagotto has a rounded head and dense curls; the Barbet has a long beard and woolly coat."},
	{"ids":["old-english-sheepdog","bearded-collie","polish-lowland-sheepdog","briard","tibetan-terrier"],"tell":"Shaggy dogs: the Old English Sheepdog is bulky and grey-white with no tail. The Beardie is lean with a parted coat. The PON is compact and smaller. The Briard is big with double dewclaws. The Tibetan Terrier has snowshoe feet."},
	{"ids":["chihuahua","russian-toy","prague-ratter","miniature-pinscher"],"tell":"The Chihuahua has an apple-domed head. The Russian Toy is leggier with big (often fringed) ears. The Prague Ratter is a tiny black-and-tan with a rounder head. The Min Pin is high-stepping and sleek."},
	{"ids":["brussels-griffon","griffon-belge","petit-brabancon","affenpinscher"],"tell":"The Belgian griffons share a face: red and rough is Brussels, black and rough is Belgian, smooth is Petit Brabançon. The Affenpinscher is black, shaggier, with a monkey face."},
	{"ids":["grand-bleu-de-gascogne","petit-bleu-de-gascogne","griffon-bleu-de-gascogne","basset-bleu-de-gascogne"],"tell":"The blue Gascony hounds differ in size and coat: Grand large, Petit smaller, Griffon rough-coated, Basset low."},
	{"ids":["anglo-francais-tricolore","anglo-francais-blanc-noir","anglo-francais-blanc-orange","french-tricolour-hound","french-white-black-hound","french-white-orange-hound"],"tell":"The big French pack hounds are told by colour: tricolour, white and black, or white and orange. The Anglo-French ones are sturdier, with English blood."},
	{"ids":["swiss-hound","small-swiss-hound"],"tell":"The same four colours: the Small Swiss Hound is the short-legged one."},
	{"ids":["hanover-hound","bavarian-mountain-hound"],"tell":"Both red with a dark mask. The Hanover is heavier and wrinkled; the Bavarian lighter and more agile."},
	{"ids":["istrian-shorthaired","istrian-coarsehaired"],"tell":"Both white with orange: smooth or rough coat."},
	{"ids":["hamiltonstovare","finnish-hound","schillerstovare","smaland-hound"],"tell":"The Hamiltonstövare and Finnish Hound are tricolour with a black saddle and white blaze. The Schillerstövare is black and tan with no white. The Småland is black and tan and compact."},
	{"ids":["czechoslovakian-wolfdog","saarloos-wolfdog","siberian-husky"],"tell":"The wolfdogs are taller and leaner than a Husky, with amber eyes; the Husky has a mask and often blue eyes."},
	{"ids":["pointer","dalmatian"],"tell":"A spotted white dog with a short coat: the Dalmatian is covered in small round spots; the Pointer has larger patches and a dished face."}
];
